  "source": "one-continuous-master",
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "line-01",
      "text": "Pinocchio started toward school, proudly carrying the primer Geppetto had sacrificed for.",
      "start": 0.064,
      "end": 6.674
    },
    {
      "id": "line-02",
      "text": "Music from a nearby puppet theater made him forget every promise.",
      "start": 6.674,
      "end": 11.697
    },
    {
      "id": "line-03",
      "text": "He sold the precious book and spent the money on a ticket.",
      "start": 11.697,
      "end": 16.387
    },
    {
      "id": "line-04",
      "text": "Onstage, the wooden actors immediately recognized Pinocchio as their long-lost brother.",
      "start": 16.387,
      "end": 23.739
    },
    {
      "id": "line-05",
      "text": "They abandoned the play and greeted him with noisy affection.",
      "start": 23.739,
      "end": 28.354
    },
    {
      "id": "line-06",
      "text": "Their enormous director, Fire Eater, entered and demanded an explanation.",
      "start": 28.354,
      "end": 34.82
    },
    {
      "id": "line-07",
      "text": "He blamed Pinocchio for the ruined performance and threatened to burn him.",
      "start": 34.82,
      "end": 39.997
    },
    {
      "id": "line-08",
      "text": "The terrified puppet called for his father and begged for mercy.",
      "start": 39.997,
      "end": 45.955
    },
    {
      "id": "line-09",
      "text": "Fire Eater's repeated sneezes revealed that his anger was beginning to soften.",
      "start": 45.955,
      "end": 51.773
    },
    {
      "id": "line-10",
      "text": "He spared Pinocchio but ordered Harlequin burned beneath the roasting dinner.",
      "start": 51.773,
      "end": 58.159
    },
    {
      "id": "line-11",
      "text": "Pinocchio refused to celebrate while his innocent friend faced danger.",
      "start": 58.159,
      "end": 64.159
    },
    {
      "id": "line-12",
      "text": "He begged, argued, and finally offered to replace Harlequin himself.",
      "start": 64.159,
      "end": 70.423
    },
    {
      "id": "line-13",
      "text": "The selfish runaway suddenly acted with loyalty and genuine courage.",
      "start": 70.423,
      "end": 76.562
    },
    {
      "id": "line-14",
      "text": "Fire Eater lifted him up, deeply moved by the sacrifice.",
      "start": 76.562,
      "end": 81.988
    },
    {
      "id": "line-15",
      "text": "He pardoned Harlequin and decided to eat his dinner uncooked.",
      "start": 81.988,
      "end": 88.024
    },
    {
      "id": "line-16",
      "text": "The entire puppet company danced with relief until dawn.",
      "start": 88.024,
      "end": 92.974
    }
  ],
